    "result_text": "Done. The full test suite is green (`BUILD SUCCESS`, 1 test, 0 failures).\n\n## Summary\n\nThe `initials` field is a computed, read-only field on the owner JSON response. I implemented it in two places:\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an `initials` read-only string property to the `Owner` schema (alongside the existing `displayName`), so the generated `OwnerDto` includes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a MapStruct `@Mapping` expression that computes it from the model:\n   ```java\n   owner.getFirstName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\" +\n   owner.getLastName().substring(0, 1).toUpperCase() + \".\"\n   ```\n   This produces the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot \u2014 e.g. `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`, matching the spec and the `coreComputesInitials` acceptance test.\n\nThis mirrors the existing `displayName` pattern already in the codebase, keeping with the conventional Spring/MapStruct idioms used throughout. Both `firstName` and `lastName` are `@NotEmpty`/required, so the `substring(0, 1)` calls are safe.",
